{
	title: 'Rotation spends the quota most at risk of expiring',
	spec: `The default account choice (pickAccount, task wf) spends weekly quota before it expires unused. Running out is acceptable; wasted quota is not.

Eligible: a subscription whose shared windows (5h, 7d; model-specific windows such as 7d_opus are ignored) are below 100% used; a 429 marks an account limited until its reset. Expired windows count as unused (usage.windows).

Need: the 7d quota left per hour until that window resets, the pace that spends it all.

Order: eligible subscriptions first, highest need first; on a tie, or for accounts without a known 7d reset (no data, or a window past its reset), the least used first, and those come after accounts with a known reset. Then the remaining subscriptions, least used first (they still work until a 429). Then API keys. pick() still skips broken and limited accounts.

A running session keeps its account (task wg) while it is eligible. It moves to the first account in the order when its account is no longer eligible, or when that account needs spending at least 25% faster than its own. The margin stops flipping, which rebuilds the prompt cache, as each account need drops with use.

Example: 2/3 with 54% left resetting in 130 h (0.42%/h) and 3/3 with 89% left resetting in 149 h (0.60%/h): 3/3 goes first although 2/3 resets sooner.

Tests: ranking by need among eligible accounts; spent accounts come after eligible ones; a session switches only past the 25% margin.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'usage.standing() gives eligible/need/used; usage.keeps(provider, mine, best) is the stickiness test pickAccount applies. Accounts without a known 7d reset rank after those with one, least used first, so a freshly reset week is spent last.',
		'Ranking by earliest 7d reset alone left an account with 89% weekly quota last because another reset 19 hours sooner with 54% left; the larger quota then risked expiring. Need (quota left per hour) fixes it. Invariant: of eligible accounts, the one whose quota is most at risk of expiring is used first.'
	],
	needs: ['61', 'wg', 'wf'],
	foldInto: ['61', 'wg']
}
